-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Treasure Island Dizzy
  Publisher   Code Masters, 1989
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Dizzy 2 - Treasure Island Dizzy (1989)(Code Masters)(128K).z80
  MD5         db6ccbeb2f9c601476efab3cfd28b131

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (+0.00% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless, the plain
              .nex as control, input keyed to the game loop 0x61A8, lockstep
              checked at every update; one busy trial in 10 lost one interrupt
              (in the game's own interrupts-off windows at another moment) and
              left lockstep at update 147)

  Changes     1.0: Dean Woodyatt's Treasure Island Dizzy build moved to the
              128K release (AY music), his hooks at 28 MHz, whole alt ROM
              image, loading screen

  Note        The 128K release, so the AY music plays. Dean Woodyatt's
              Treasure Island Dizzy builder: Dizzy is four hardware sprites,
              so he no longer takes the colours of the scenery he walks
              through; his hooks now run at 28 MHz. Loading screen from the
              tape.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Immunity

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

