-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-05: approved

  Replay      4 recordings of the 128K release IDENTICAL on rework v128 (3 bot
              walks of 12,035 / 12,000 / 12,011 frames, and 1,103 frames on
              the sea bed with the .pok's walk-in-water POKE to reach the
              bubbles): 6,927 plots pixel-perfect, 6,900 erases, 27,567 ISR
              hide checks, 111 room wipes, 189 bubble tests (the virtual read)
              equal to the original's; the game never touches the trampolines
              in the printer buffer; 3 negative controls detected; clock
              matrix 5 hook sites x 4 incoming clocks = 20 cases PASS, a
              forced 3.5 MHz exit detected; ROM paths: every ROM byte as
              recorded; start-up tail never read before written

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: loading screen, title, play reached,
              frames viewed; AY music written (469-550 data writes a second,
              as the original); flicker 300 frames: 0 out of step, 0 vanished,
              0 transients; 15-minute soak against the original .z80: no
              freeze, loop or crash; no person played it

  Coverage    the first rooms and the sea bed only (bot walks); inventory and
              dialogue boxes not opened by the bots (the TID engine has no box
              routine here); loading screen stub in bank 13, emulator-tested
              only; cheats proved in the simulator on the original 128K file:
              Immunity: the hazard death routine 0x7269 returns at once (4,906
              calls on one walk), Dizzy went through 24 room changes against 4
              before a game over (drowning still kills); dropped: Walk in
              water (the game reset into BASIC at frame 1,130 of a walk with
              it), Walk through walls (no effect seen walking left or right
              for 3,000 frames), Cheat mode (use key C) (its effect not
              established: Dizzy vanished), Immunity (alt) (0x742A is text in
              this release)

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
